From 88a8ab4f36dc4db24af24c5dfb5597d03c37ff01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:11:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 102/197] Unified: the design check shows its progress, can be
 cancelled, and does not freeze the GUI

The overlap of each pair of parts can take seconds, and while OCC computes
FreeCAD does not take mouse input. In the GUI the pairs are now computed in
a separate FreeCADCmd process (shapes passed as BREP files, one JSON line
per pair), so the view stays usable; cancelling ends the process. The
panel shows what is being checked and 'n / m pairs' with a Cancel button
(also for 'Fix all'), the status bar shows 'Checking n/m' with a Stop
button. Scripts and the CLI still check in the same process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
